Base sprite for a pixel-art game character (shown at 1x, 4x, 8x on grey). Chibi swordswoman, SE (front 3/4, facing down-right) view, ~48px tall in a 64x64 cell. Design: dark bob with straight bangs, small bun at back, big red bow, big blue eyes set low, red short kimono-dress with flared hem and wide sleeves, one dark obi, pale legs, dark boots. This sprite will be cut into parts (head, bow, torso, sleeves, skirt, legs) for a cutout pixel rig. Critique it strictly as hand-made pixel art: silhouette at 1x, 3/4 view read (does the head/face read as turned to SE?), outline quality (jaggies, doubles, banding), shading (pillow shading?), clusters/orphans, sleeve and leg shapes, proportions/appeal. Give a prioritized list of concrete per-pixel or per-region fixes.
